# Reset PostgreSQL Password Plan

## Goal Description
The user cannot authenticate to the local PostgreSQL database because the `postgres` user password is unknown or incorrect. The goal is to reset this password to `password` (and enable the `test` user) to allow the application to connect.

## User Review Required
> [!WARNING]
> This process involves modifying [pg_hba.conf](file:///C:/Program%20Files/PostgreSQL/18/data/pg_hba.conf) in your PostgreSQL installation directory. This is a system configuration file.
> We will temporarily change authentication method to `trust` (no password), reset the password, and then change it back to `scram-sha-256` (password required).

## Proposed Changes
### PostgreSQL Configuration
#### [MODIFY] [pg_hba.conf](file:///C:/Program Files/PostgreSQL/18/data/pg_hba.conf)
- Temporarily change `host all all 127.0.0.1/32 scram-sha-256` to `host all all 127.0.0.1/32 trust`
- Temporarily change `host all all ::1/128 scram-sha-256` to `host all all ::1/128 trust`

### Database
- Reset password for user `postgres` to `password`.
- Create user `test` with password `test` (as requested originally).
- Create database `ghg_enterprise` if it doesn't exist.

## Verification Plan
### Automated Verification
1.  Run `node check_pg_db.js` to verify connection with `postgres`/`password`.
2.  Run `node check_pg_db.js` (modified for `test` user) to verify `test`/`test`.

### Manual Verification
- User will run the provided batch scripts and confirm successful connection.
